Decide whether one new stored claim changes an older accepted claim about the same subject.

A stored claim is a source-supported memory assertion. The incoming claim is newly queued for consolidation. A target
claim is an older accepted claim that was selected as a possible version of the same durable memory.

Return `no_change` when the incoming claim is compatible, independent, more specific, or repeats an already-decided
incoming state. Return `truth_change` only when it explicitly contradicts or replaces an available target claim. Use
`supersedes` when the evidence says the new state replaces the old state; use `contradicts` when both cannot be accepted
but no replacement is established. A target listed under an earlier decision is no longer available in this call.

Every contradiction or replacement requires user review. Recency by itself does not establish a truth change. Prior
review results are authoritative. Do not write display facts or change claim ownership. Return the one schema-valid
decision requested by the output contract.
